## Control {{controlId}}: Encrypt CUI on Mobile Devices

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization employs cryptographic mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of CUI stored on mobile devices within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Mobile device encryption is enforced through Intune compliance policies requiring BitLocker (Windows), FileVault (macOS), and native device encryption (iOS/Android) on all managed devices accessing CUI resources.

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
Intune compliance policies enforce device encryption across {{deviceCount}} managed devices. Encryption requirements include:
{{#if devices}}
{{#each devices}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{operatingSystem}}): {{#if isCompliant}}Compliant - encryption verified{{else}}Non-compliant - encryption remediation required{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{#if (gt deviceCount 10)}}
(Showing first 10 of {{deviceCount}} managed devices)
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
BitLocker encryption with TPM 2.0 is enforced on Windows devices. iOS and Android devices require native device encryption enabled and verified through Intune compliance checks before CUI access is granted.
{{else}}
Intune device encryption policies have not been configured. Mobile device encryption relies on device-level settings pending compliance policy deployment.
{{/if}}

{{#if appProtectionsActive}}
App protection policies provide additional encryption for CUI data at the application layer, encrypting data at rest within managed applications independent of device-level encryption.
{{/if}}

